face paint protection, windshield protection, and automotive and architectural window films, as well as proprietary DAP software. The company also provides pre-cut film products, merchandise and apparel, ceramic coatings, installation, and tools and accessories; and training services to customers for the installation of its products. In addition, the company offers paint protection kits, car wash products, after-care products, and installation tools through its website. The company sells and distributes its products through independent installers, new car dealerships, third-party distributors, automobile original equipment manufacturers, and company-owned installation centers, as well as through franchisees and online channels. The company operates in the United States, Canada, China, the Asia Pacific, European Union, the United Kingdom, Africa, India, the Middle East, Latin America, and internationally. XPEL, Inc. was founded in 1997 and is headquartered in San Antonio, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ryan L. Pape | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 43 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $356K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $47K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["XPEL, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.0B market cap on $476M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 38% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 28-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $63M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.31\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.5% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 23% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Shares offer a 18% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"XPEL's (NASDAQ:XPEL) Earnings Are Of Questionable Quality","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nasdaq-xpel/xpel/news/xpels-nasdaqxpel-earnings-are-of-questionable-quality","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575178.345,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why XPEL (XPEL) Is Up 5.3% And What's Next","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nasdaq-xpel/xpel/news/why-xpel-xpel-is-up-53-and-whats-next","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794364572.26,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"XPEL (NASDAQ:XPEL) Stock Jumps 4.9% \u2013 Still a Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/xpel-nasdaqxpel-stock-jumps-4-9-still-a-buy.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794335072.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"XPEL (XPEL) Could Be 38% Undervalued On Third Quarter 2026 Results","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nasdaq-xpel/xpel/news/xpel-xpel-could-be-38-undervalued-on-third-quarter-2026-resu","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794212520.441,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.849,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"XPEL Fell While Profit Rose","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nasdaq-xpel/xpel/news/xpel-fell-while-profit-rose","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794029313.847,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"XPEL Reports Q3 2026 Revenue of $137.8M and EPS of $0.59","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/xpel-reports-q3-2026-revenue-of-1378m-and-eps-of-059","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973032.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["ea