he top four hold 26% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted higher, up 12% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 25% over the last three months.","The price sits near the bottom of its 52-week range, 32% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 41% and a beta of 1.07, it moves roughly with the market.","About $8.4M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 51% in the 2020 crash and 43% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 18% below its DCF fair value of $46.34, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 14%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $31.72 to $68.52 (P10-P90).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 30% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 6.0% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $57.00 on average, 51% above the price.","The price implies 13.1% annual cash-flow growth, 4pp less than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 38% clears the cost of capital of 9.9% by 28pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.39).","It runs a 39% gross margin and converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.31x.","ROE of 18% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.4x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.6% of revenue on R&D and 0.6% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 9.7, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 3.25).","Working capital ties up about 151 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 13.7% over 3 years and 24.5% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","At current returns, reinvesting 61% of profits supports about 22.8% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 30.4% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 484%.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (0.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 37, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 9.5%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 88%.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.3% (0.3% in buybacks).","Short interest is elevated at 15.6% of the float, 15.9 days to cover."],"people":["With about 1,337 employees, each generates about $356K of revenue, in line with the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 24.2% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $47K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.2M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":91,"head":"Invest: trades 18% below fair value of $46.34; ROIC 37.6% vs WACC 9.9%.","pros":["Composite 63, above the 57 line (gates 18/25)","Trades 18% below fair value of $46.34","ROIC 37.6% vs WACC 9.9%","FCF margin 13.2%","Revenue grew 24.5%/yr over 5y"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":39.39,"vc":{"base":46.34,"base_src":"dcf","bear":31.72,"bull":68.52,"alt_median":35.72,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.2972,"dispersion":0.1417,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"mc_quantiles":[24.25,28.69,31.72,34.22,36.78,38.35,39.88,41.59,43.04,44.57,46.69,48.74,50.15,52.13,54.56,56.87,59.86,63.78,68.52,75.88,92.2],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.782,"discount_rate":0.175,"terminal_growth":0.008,"exit_multiple":0.036},"ticker":"XPEL","date":"2026-11-13"}